(Process & Strategy Log) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Empowerment) Tj
T*
(Before this exercise, my software-building ability depended heavily on technical fluency:) Tj
T*
(writing syntax from scratch, remembering framework conventions, and debugging implementation) Tj
T*
(details line by line. That made turning ideas into working software slower and often) Tj
T*
(intimidating when the scope expanded quickly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(After this exercise, the process felt more like product direction and systems thinking. I could) Tj
T*
(describe intent \(for example, "add track sectors and A/B comparison modes"\), evaluate outputs,) Tj
T*
(and iterate toward a result without needing to manually author every line first. This was) Tj
T*
(meaningfully empowering because the tool reduced the gap between concept and implementation.) Tj
T*
(Instead of getting blocked on low-level details, I focused on defining behavior, reviewing) Tj
T*
(outputs, and deciding trade-offs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(It was also occasionally overwhelming: the tool can generate large changes quickly, and if) Tj
T*
(prompts are broad, outputs may drift from intent. The key learning is that non-coders get the) Tj
T*
(most value when they treat this as guided collaboration, not one-shot magic. Practical habits) Tj
T*
(include:) Tj
T*
(- breaking requests into clear features;) Tj
T*
(- validating each increment in the UI;) Tj
T*
(- asking for explicit constraints \(data model, edge cases, UX expectations\);) Tj
T*
(- requiring explainability \("what changed and why"\);) Tj
T*
(- preserving a feedback loop \(test -> critique -> refine\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(In short, this tool can materially empower non-coders to ship tangible outcomes, provided they) Tj
T*
(use structured prompting and active review.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Iterative development) Tj
T*
(I evaluated outputs through repeated small loops:) Tj
T*
(1. define feature intent and acceptance criteria;) Tj
T*
(2. inspect generated code/UI behavior;) Tj
T*
(3. run syntax checks and manual smoke tests;) Tj
T*
(4. identify mismatches or bugs;) Tj
T*
(5. refine prompts/rules and re-run.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Examples of refinement strategies used:) Tj
T*
(- **Granular requirements:** Instead of "improve comparison," I specified compare modes,) Tj
T*
(baseline presets, and swap behavior.) Tj
T*
(- **Business-rule clarification:** I encoded constraints like valid compare-car selection \(no) Tj
T*
(self-comparison\) and saved-state compatibility.) Tj
T*
(- **Model grounding:** I requested explicit factors \(tire warmup windows, ambient penalties,) Tj
T*
(sector-level gain/loss\) so simulation behavior remained interpretable.) Tj
T*
(- **Persistence expectations:** I required settings/profile state to survive reloads and) Tj
T*
(imports.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(These strategies improved outcome quality by reducing ambiguity, surfacing edge cases earlier,) Tj
T*
(and making generated logic easier to audit. The final app is richer and more stable because) Tj
T*
(iteration was treated as a controlled product-development cycle rather than a single prompt.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Organizational Trade-offs) Tj
T*
(Benefits:) Tj
T*
(- **Agility:** teams can prototype internal tools and workflow automations much faster.) Tj
T*
(- **Accessibility:** more employees can translate domain knowledge into functional software.) Tj
T*
(- **Experimentation:** low-friction iteration enables faster discovery and validation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Risks:) Tj
T*
(- **Security/compliance drift:** rapid local tools may bypass standard review controls.) Tj
T*
(- **Maintainability debt:** ungoverned "vibe-coded" apps can accumulate inconsistent patterns.) Tj
T*
(- **Operational fragility:** ownership ambiguity, missing tests, and weak documentation can) Tj
T*
(increase long-term risk.) Tj
T*
() Tj
